                                "example_id": "ae945cb9-9145-4f43-a643-e235607c6c82",
                                "sense_id": "b886d016-6da2-3185-8aa0-616ca6ad42e7",
                                "text": "She is one of our outcasts; a common prostitute, who obtains from the wages of promiscuous intercourse her daily bread; who sells for hire, in unenjoying prostitution, the feminine embraces given by Nature for mutual solace and endearment."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fc69cd8-7fc1-4fc1-aa48-5724ad0cbf54",
                                "sense_id": "b886d016-6da2-3185-8aa0-616ca6ad42e7",
                                "text": "1871-2, George Eliot, Middlemarch\nThe coachman was used to drive his grays at a good pace, Mr Casaubon being unenjoying and impatient in everything away from his desk, and wanting to get to the end of all journeys; and Dorothea was now bowled along quickly."
                            }
                        ]
